Subject: [EXPERIMENT, NOT DEVICE-VERIFIED] Skip ELF linker-notifier hooks on TiVo test build

Equivalent source-level behavior of the two-byte ARM32 Gadget edit.
Base: frida/frida-gum tag 17.9.1.
This source patch is provided for review; the delivered APK uses the guarded
binary edit in repack_tivo_test2.py, not a recompiled Frida build.

Limitation: module tracking stops after initial enumeration/synchronization.
This intentionally skips all ELF rtld notifiers in this test engine and is
not a general upstream fix for failed code-deflector allocation.

--- a/gum/backend-elf/gummoduleregistry-elf.c
+++ b/gum/backend-elf/gummoduleregistry-elf.c
@@ -103,6 +103,9 @@
 gum_hook_rtld_notifier (const GumRtldNotifierDetails * details,
                         gpointer user_data)
 {
+  /* TiVo test 2: avoid installing a linker hook before Gadget config loads. */
+  return;
+
   gpointer impl = details->location;
 #if defined (HAVE_I386) || defined (HAVE_ARM64)
   G_GNUC_UNUSED cs_insn * first_instruction;
